// Personal Debug signing overrides — OPTIONAL.
//
// Copy this file to Config/Local.xcconfig (which is gitignored) to sign Debug builds
// with your own Apple Developer team instead of the default ad-hoc ("Sign to Run
// Locally"). You only need this if you're testing entitlements that require a real
// team (e.g. some App Group / push scenarios). For ordinary local development you can
// ignore this file entirely.
//
// Signing-Debug.xcconfig does `#include? "Local.xcconfig"` after its defaults, so
// anything you set here wins.
//
// TIP — keep TCC permissions across rebuilds: the default ad-hoc identity ("-") produces a
// new signature every build, so macOS resets Accessibility / Full Disk Access / Calendar
// grants each rebuild. Signing Debug with a STABLE identity (any code-signing cert in your
// keychain — e.g. your "Apple Development: <you>" cert) keeps those grants. List identities:
//   security find-identity -v -p codesigning
// then set the exact name below (Manual signing; no provisioning profile is needed for a
// locally-run Mac app). You re-grant permissions once after switching; then they stick.

// CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Manual
// CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = Apple Development: Your Name (TEAMID)
// CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY[sdk=macosx*] = Apple Development: Your Name (TEAMID)

// DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = ABCDE12345
// CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Automatic
// CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = Apple Development
